88 [303.18]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">87 [81.16]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">124 [125.33]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">102 [78.29]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">50 [54.04]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">50 [34.34]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">33 [22.32]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">734 [698.66]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.07</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.83 (&#x02212;0.10&#x02013;1.12)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Circulatory ex CeVD</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1820 [1877.49]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">481 [456.88]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">709 [702.81]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">522 [453.09]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">337 [312.61]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">271 [201.97]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">161 [122.78]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4301 [4127.62]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.72 (0.39&#x02013;1.10)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="11" rowspan="1"><bold>Underlying and contributory causes</bold></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Diabetes</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">125 [133.13]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48 [35.68]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">54 [57.60]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">42 [39.86]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">40 [28.99]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">26 [20.85]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">24 [14.54]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">359 [330.64]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.038</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.15 (0.20&#x02013;2.56)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Circulatory diseases</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2663 [2731.73]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">732 [692.83]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1106 [1095.65]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">769 [717.81]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">549 [496.16]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">400 [327.50]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">257 [203.17]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6476 [6264.83]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.54 (0.30&#x02013;0.82)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;IHD</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1745 [1786.72]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">473 [439.96]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">678 [682.23]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">492 [448.09]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">354 [312.77]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">259 [204.48]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">164 [123.20]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4165 [3997.44]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.70 (0.37&#x02013;1.07)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;CeVD</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">506 [521.21]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">152 [146.90]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">261 [244.80]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">169 [164.34]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">130 [110.50]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">79 [72.25]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">68 [46.97]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1365 [1306.96]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.02</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.66 (0.17&#x02013;1.27)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Respiratory diseases</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1060 [1086.44]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">327 [314.05]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">522 [513.13]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">356 [344.74]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">259 [228.95]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">164 [152.59]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">125 [99.04]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2813 [2738.93]</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.04</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.40 (0.07&#x02013;0.79)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>IHD: ischaemic heart disease; CeVD: cerebro vascular disease.</p></fn><fn id="TF1"><p><sup>a</sup>Excluding accidents and violence.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></p><p>As internal radiation workers will have also received doses from internally incorporated radionuclides, and as our stratification according to industrial or non-industrial employment status may only crudely reflect differences in background mortality due to socio-economic factors, we have also examined the mortality experience of the four subgroups of radiation exposure and employment status separately (<xref ref-type="table" rid="T5">Table 5</xref>, <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://ije.oxfordjournals.org/cgi/content/full/dyn018/DC1">Supplementary Data C</ext-link>).<table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Linear excess relative risk coefficients for the four categories of employment and radiation exposure status</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead align="left"><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" colspan="5" rowspan="1">ERR Sv<sup>&#x02212;1</sup> (number of deaths, 90% CI)</th></tr><tr><th rowspan="